\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14.1}{\ignorespaces The six levels of evidence used in this book. Lower levels contain many small cases and are cheap to repeat; higher levels contain few cases and test more of the stack at once. A higher level does not replace a lower one: it can pass while a component below it is wrong in a region it does not visit.\relax }}{139}{figure.caption.246}\protected@file@percent }
